Classify each triangle by its side properties.
(a) The matching ticks show equal sides. The side $BC$ has a different length from $AB$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9,draw=black]
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (A) at (1.4,3.2);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.8,0);
\draw[tickmark] (A)--(B);
\draw[tickmark] (A)--(C);
\draw (B)--(C);
\node[above] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) A triangle has sides $7$ cm, $10$ cm and $12$ cm.

Use the marks and vertex letters in this triangle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9,draw=black]
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (J) at (0.3,1);
\coordinate (K) at (3.3,1);
\coordinate (L) at (3.3,4);
\draw[tickmark] (J)--(K);
\draw[tickmark] (K)--(L);
\draw (L)--(J);
\coordinate (ka) at ($(K)!0.3cm!(J)$);
\coordinate (kb) at ($(K)!0.3cm!(L)$);
\draw (ka)--($(ka)+(kb)-(K)$)--(kb);
\node[below left] at (J) {$J$};
\node[below right] at (K) {$K$};
\node[above right] at (L) {$L$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Name the triangle starting at $L$ and reading clockwise.
(b) Name the equal sides and the equal angles.
(c) Classify the triangle by its sides and its angles.
(d) Name the angle opposite $JK$.

Classify each triangle by its sides and its angles.
(a) The matching ticks show equal sides.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.5,2.598076);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (1.5,-0.12)--(1.5,0.12);
\draw (0.646077,1.359038)--(0.853923,1.239038);
\draw (2.146077,1.239038)--(2.353923,1.359038);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) A triangle has angles $48^{\circ}$, $57^{\circ}$ and $75^{\circ}$.
